Z||000012||merlin||08-13-2001||10:37 PM||||I’m at a loss for words…  I own a 1987 Fiero GT and a 1995 Ford Probe GT and I am a member of both forums. I’m not sure what side of the fence to jump onto.  I love both these cars and there are obviously good and bad points regarding both these vehicles.  Overall, the cost of maintenance on the Probe is somewhat high compared to the Fiero, but both are a b***h to work on.  The stock V6 performance of both cars is respectable, with a slight edge going to the Probe if both drivers were comparable.  <P>I think one of my biggest complaints for both vehicles is the sometimes unjustified public perception of both of them…<BR>Probe:<BR>‘You know your not really driving an American car it’s  got a rice engine’.<BR>“You paid that much for your Probe, it’s not even worth half that now.” <P>Fiero:<BR>“Doesn’t that car catch fire”<BR>“Isn’t that car made of plastic”<P>Again, I think both these cars are great and I plan on keeping both of them for years to come.<BR>||||reg||2
