Z||000023||frontal lobe||08-14-2001||02:24 PM||||Well, I never had a probe GT, but I had a Mazda 626 and I believe the GT had the same 2.2liter turbo-charged, intercooled engine.  If so, in straight-line acceleration, my 626 turbo would have whooped up on my '87 Fiero GT.  The problem is, though, that you can't do "straight-line" acceleration in a powerful front-drive car.  When I would get on that car from a start, it would torque-steer all over the place and leave me hanging on for dear life.  While it was fun in an "amusement-park ride"-like way, it really limited when I could get on it for safety reasons.  I'd need to make sure I had about 2 lanes clear (OK, slight exageration to make the point).<P>The latest Prove v6 vs. my Fiero-I'd have to go with the Fiero.<P>But these are just observations-all irrelevant.  You like what you like.   People are different.  They have different tastes.  What is it with some people that can't let you like something different without trying to put you down?||||reg||1
