Z||000025||Ditz88GT||08-14-2001||04:11 PM||||Frontal Lobe, Your completely right about the 2.2 turbo in the Probe.  I did have one, well actually two, one turbo one not.  the non-turbo was very slow.  Much much slower than a duke Fiero.  (I know because I raced a 4cyl Fiero when I had mine and got my a$$ handed to me) Same motor, just no turbo.  As for the turbo GT I had...wow.  It was a very fast car, I would guess even faster than my 88 GT.  But once again you are exactly right about the torque-steer.  It was a lot of car to hold down.  I want to make on thing clear, I did like my Probe GT, but would never trade my Fiero for one.  Just my opinion.  Anyway, as for the 2nd generation...they did improve the looks and from what I've heard the handling.  But there is no way a bone stock 2nd gen Probe GT would even come close to hanging with a V6 fiero.  Seems they really dropped the ball with the new power plant.<P>Just my 2 cents<P><P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT<BR>http://go.to/fiero||||reg||1
Z||000026||Leadfoot||08-14-2001||04:35 PM||||I guess it is in their nature to probe around.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  O.k. I'll stop know...man do I love this cable modem.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Fformula88||08-14-2001||04:46 PM||||I think they are a lot closer in performance than a lot of people here are giving them credit for.  The 2nd gen GT's will hang right with a Fiero.  The Fiero's tested in the low 8's high 7's in 0-60 and very high 15's to low 16's in 1/4 mile in magazine road tests.  93+ Probe GT's were in the mid to upper 7's with high 15 to low 16's in the 1/4.<P>I know test numbers can very because of a lot of factors, but they are both neck and neck if you factor in all the test numbers.<P>Like Merlin, I also own examples of both, my 88 Formula and a 97 PSE (4-cyl).  My 4 banger auto Probe will easily take a duke Fiero with an auto.  Both cars were compromised designs from the start that were killed because corporate gave up on them.  They do have a lot in common.  There biggest problem is near total lack of aftermarket support, and that includes normal replacement parts.  Going to Ford for everything gets very pricey. <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000028||b lo 0||08-14-2001||04:55 PM||||Just goes to show that we are a bit more mature here, considering the average Probe was given to little Johnny by Mommie and Daddy.  I just wish they were as cool with Fieros as most of the MR2 guys are (MrBad should not be used as a benchmark for all Mister drivers).  Hey, if they wanna be passionate about their cars, go for it, just leave my beloved Fiero out of it.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
